functional requirement:
[OUTPUT] ## general overview of the project The task is to develop a comprehensive web application, 'OnlineVintageMarket', for buying and selling vintage items that utilizes Python and stores information in local text files, eliminating the need for SQL databases. Note that the website should start from the login page. ## software functional requirements 1. Users shall be able to log in to their accounts on the Login Page. 2. Users shall be able to navigate to the Registration Page via the Register here link if they do not have an account. 3. Users shall be able to view available vintage items on the Home Page. 4. Users shall be able to search for specific vintage items by name using the search bar on the Home Page. 5. Users shall be able to view details of a selected item by clicking the "Item Details" button on the Home Page. 6. Users shall be able to create a new listing for vintage items by navigating to the Listing Page and entering the item name, description, and price. 7. Users shall be able to submit their item listings through the "Submit Listing" button on the Listing Page. 8. Users shall be able to view detailed information about a vintage item, including its title, description, and price, on the Item Details Page. 9. Users shall be able to navigate back to the Home Page from the Item Details Page using the "Back" button. [/OUTPUT]

